{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.921,
   "text": "I spent one winter alone at a mountain observatory, keeping the big telescope running through the night."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.521,
   "end": 16.025,
   "text": "Beside the eyepiece hung an old star chart... and one rule, written in the margin."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.625,
   "end": 21.02,
   "text": "If you ever see a star that isn't on this chart... close the dome."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.62,
   "end": 26.164,
   "text": "Don't point the telescope at it. And never let it see the dome open."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.064,
   "end": 32.056,
   "text": "For two months, the sky matched that chart perfectly. Every single night."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 33.056,
   "end": 40.245,
   "text": "Then, one night in January, I found it. A cold, white star, low over the pines... where the chart showed nothing."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 40.845,
   "end": 44.749,
   "text": "I told myself it was a plane. A satellite. Anything."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 45.649,
   "end": 49.148,
   "text": "But it didn't drift across the sky like the others..."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.548,
   "end": 52.916,
   "text": "It just kept getting brighter."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.916,
   "end": 57.945,
   "text": "I slammed the switch to close the dome."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.545,
   "end": 63.215,
   "text": "The motor groaned... and the roof stopped, halfway shut."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.415,
   "end": 68.316,
   "text": "Through the gap, the new star blinked."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 70.316,
   "end": 76.289,
   "text": "Then a second one opened right beside it... and both of them looked down. Into the dome. At me."
  }
 ],
